applies to.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Defines the line range in the original host file that the snippet information
applies to.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;This field defines the line range in the original host file that the snippet
information applies to.

If there is a disagreement between the byte range and line range, the byte
range values will take precedence.

A range of lines is a convenient reference for those files where there is a
known line delimiter.
The choice was made to start the numbering of the lines at 1 to be consistent
with the W3C pointer method vocabulary.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
